    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Opposition view",
          "heading": "Italy prop Simone Ferrari rates improved Fiji no easier than Argentina",
          "body": "Asked in Udine whether Saturday's Nations Championship meeting would be easier than last weekend's 14-19 home defeat to Argentina, Italy prop Simone Ferrari answered flatly that it would not. He described Fiji as an improved, solid side on the rise, with many players based in France and plenty of physicality. Ferrari called Italy's scrum a well-honed weapon and wants the Azzurri to match the intensity they showed against Argentina. Fiji arrive after a 15-43 defeat to Ireland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Bluenergy Stadium, Udine"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Five-try wing Will Joseph in line to start against New Zealand",
          "body": "Gloucester's Will Joseph is understood to be in pole position to keep the wing berth for Saturday's Nations Championship meeting with the All Blacks, with wing Immanuel Feyi-Waboso ruled out of the autumn by an ankle injury. Last weekend's 78-15 win over Japan was only Joseph's second cap, four and a half years after his debut against Australia in July 2022, and he became the fifth England men's player to score five tries in one match. Cadan Murley, the squad's other specialist wing, is his rival for the spot."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection clue",
          "heading": "Matthieu Jalibert steers France at fly-half in first training run before Argentina",
          "body": "Rugbyrama's report from Tuesday's first full session at Marcoussis found one certainty: the fly-half will run France's game against the Pumas, restoring a conventional halves pairing after the improvisation that put captain Antoine Dupont at 10 against South Africa. Dupont was back at scrum-half in a near-unchanged backline, though outside back Aaron Grandidier-Nkanang was spared and his Pau teammate Grégoire Arfeuil took his place. Bib swaps among the forwards threw up surprises. France must beat Argentina to be sure of a place in the Nations Championship final in London."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stade de France, Paris"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Citing dismissed",
          "heading": "Sam Prendergast cleared to face Springboks after hip-drop citing is dismissed",
          "body": "The fly-half had faced a potential ban for a tackle on Fiji captain Peceli Yato in last Saturday's 43-15 win. He was cited under a new offence added to Law 9.13 this month. At Tuesday's hearing, an independent committee unanimously threw the case out after evidence from the 23-year-old and submissions from Ireland head coach Andy Farrell, leaving him available for Saturday's Nations Championship test. South Africa head coach Rassie Erasmus, now serving a six-match ban, had predicted Prendergast would escape punishment \"on a technicality\" while condemning the tackle itself."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Aviva Stadium, Dublin"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Head to head",
          "heading": "Italy chase first Nations Championship win against Fiji with series level six-all",
          "body": "Head coach Gonzalo Quesada's Italy face a Fiji side who, like them, are still looking for a first win in the competition. Both sit bottom of their respective pools going into Saturday's Round 6 test in Udine. The 12 previous meetings have split six wins apiece, and the last, in November 2017, went Italy's way 19-10 in Catania. Fiji arrive off a defeat by Ireland in Dublin, where they were held scoreless in the second half. OnRugby rates it likely the two meet again on the final weekend in London."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
