      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury cover",
          "heading": "Bautista Bernasconi steps up from Argentina XV to score in Genoa win",
          "body": "Picked for the Argentina XV rather than the Pumas, the Benetton hooker started last Saturday's 19-14 win over Italy only because Julián Montoya, Ignacio Ruiz and Leonel Oviedo were all injured, then scored from a maul as Argentina levelled at 7-7 by half-time. The casualty list runs deeper: Thomas Gallo, Santiago Grondona, Marcos Kremer and Joaquín Oviedo are also injured, and with Santiago Carreras and Juan Cruz Mallía both out, Bautista Delguy moved to fly-half during Tomás Albornoz's sin-bin spell."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt."
