      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching scrutiny",
          "heading": "Planet Rugby column questions Les Kiss's authority after Wallabies' Murrayfield defeat",
          "body": "Wallabies head coach Les Kiss is clearly useful, Planet Rugby's columnist allows — but as a specialist or assistant, not the man in charge. Watching Kiss speak after Sunday's 15-12 Nations Championship loss to Scotland at Murrayfield, the writer saw nothing to suggest he has the standing to sell a vision to the team or the Australian public. Nor, the piece argues, will 'sugar-hits' such as Sydney Roosters pair Mark Nawaqanitawase and Angus Crichton heading to union fix a side that needs forwards and a reliable fly-half."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Springboks coach Rassie Erasmus banned for six matches",
          "body": "Ireland's Sam Prendergast cleared of hip-drop citation before Springboks test. Scotland captain Tuipulotu out with knee injury, White also hurt. Argentina casualty list grows as Gallo, Kremer, Grondona hurt."
        }
      ],
