      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-19",
      "edition": "Thursday 19 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury call-ups",
          "heading": "Moriyama and Brua returned home injured before Japan's Twickenham defeat to England",
          "body": "Rugby Asia 247 reported on 12 November, two days before the England match, that squad member Miu Austin Moriyama and left wing Inoke Brua had returned to Japan with injuries. Faulua Makisi of Kubota Spears and Jone Naikabra of Toshiba Brave Lupus were called up as replacements. Brua's wing berth went to another Toshiba man, Rinku Tokito, selected by head coach Eddie Jones to make his debut in a side that went on to lose 15-78 at Twickenham."
        },
